# 3. NON-NEGOTIABLE DEVELOPMENT PRINCIPLES

Follow these principles throughout development.

### 3.1 Build actual functionality

Do not create buttons that do nothing.

Do not create decorative charts pretending to display real telemetry.

Do not create agent cards that claim agents are operational when no agent implementation exists.

Every interactive element must have a defined behavior.

Every data visualization must have an identifiable data source.

Every workflow must have an actual implementation or an explicitly identified simulation adapter.

### 3.2 No incomplete deliverables

Do not stop after generating:

- A landing page.
- A sidebar.
- A command center.
- A collection of static cards.
- A frontend prototype.

Build the entire application in planned, testable stages.

### 3.3 Inspect before modifying

If a repository already exists:

1. Inspect its complete directory structure.
2. Identify the framework and dependencies.
3. Read existing implementation files.
4. Understand the current architecture.
5. Identify existing functionality.
6. Preserve useful working code.
7. Identify incomplete or broken functionality.
8. Establish an implementation plan.

Never blindly overwrite an existing project.

### 3.4 No fabricated capabilities

Clearly distinguish:

- Live telemetry.
- Historical telemetry.
- Simulated telemetry.
- AI-generated analysis.
- Verified security findings.
- Proposed actions.
- Human-approved actions.
- Successfully executed actions.

Never label simulated information as live intelligence.

